#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198099 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198252 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2993b4ab-e45b-579a-8a11-b5e9ee107d5b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/id #uuid "d40cb0df-fce7-5236-b0ef-62f5a343b3a3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12724" :question/problem "Consider the following compound predicates:\n\n$x$ is even **and** divisible by $5.$ \n\n$x$ is even **or** less than $6$.\n\nExpress these compound predicates above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $A(x):$ $x$ is even\n\n- $B(x):$ $x$ is divisible by $5$\n\n- $C(x):$ $x$ is less than $6$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land.$\" \n\nSo, the first sentence reads\n\n![](images/0c/0c81e18633c3089e7c9f56464738a57dae490c70a0c8b46d116b1a8d75cd433f.svg)\n\nthat is, $A \\land B.$\n\nMoreover, the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor.$\" \n\nSo, the second sentence reads\n\n![](images/0a/0a76866dfc078172503784c3d67c7d36abbfe3362a9af3e07e6055f168debbf4.svg)\n\nthat is, $A \\lor C.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198100 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198253 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce659c55-ca26-52c6-b15e-ec317013d856" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Nested Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/id #uuid "3e2319b4-ab10-50ef-845b-9586c9761227" :question/math-academy-id "e-12725" :question/problem "Consider the following compound predicate:\n\n$x$ is positive **and** a multiple of $4,$ **or** $x$ is negative.\n\nExpress this compound predicate in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is positive\n\n- $M(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $4$\n\n- $N(x):$ $x$ is negative" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land,$\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $x$ is positive and a multiple of $4.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x \\,\\textrm{is positive}}_P \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textrm{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \\underbrace{x \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a multiple of }4 }_M,\n$$\n\nthat is, $P \\land M.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is negative. This corresponds to $N.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x \\,\\textrm{ is positive}\\,\\textrm{and a multiple of }4 }_{P \\land M} \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textrm{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \\underbrace{x \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is negative} }_N,\n$$\n\nthat is, $(P \\land M) \\lor N.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198101 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198254 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6bc626a-9517-584c-bf55-8653227f830e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Sets of Conjunctions and Disjunctions"}] :question/id #uuid "3a115dd5-3241-5627-bb40-121b75eeb7ae" :question/math-academy-id "e-12726" :question/problem "Find the truth set of $P(x) \\lor Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the universal set $\\mathbb{R}{:}$\n\n- $P(x):$ $3x -1 < 5$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x \\geq 3$" :question/worked-solution "The truth set of $P(x) \\lor Q(x)$ represents the *union* of the truth sets of $P(x)$ and $Q(x){:}$\n\n$$\nT_{P \\lor Q} = T_P \\cup T_Q\n$$\n\nWe start by finding the truth sets of $P(x)$ and $Q(x){:}$\n\n- To find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-1 & <5 \\\\ 3x & <6 \\\\ x & <2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is\n$T_P = (-\\infty,2).$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n$T_Q = [3,\\infty).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P∨Q} & ={T}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,2)\\cup [3,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198104 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198255 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f674fcf-7f3e-53c0-8759-6f83b0820160" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Conjunction and Disjunction"}] :question/id #uuid "2ab89571-f4e2-515f-9d01-b1213e73ffc0" :question/math-academy-id "e-12733" :question/problem "Write a sentence that is equivalent to the following: \"$x$ is an integer, and $x$ is negative and it is an integer.\"" :question/worked-solution "Using the commutative law, we can replace the phrase \"$x$ is negative and it is an integer\" with the phrase \"$x$ is an integer and it is negative.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is an integer, and $x$ is an integer and it is negative.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma:\n\n\"$x$ is an integer and $x$ is an integer, and it is negative.\"\n\nNow, we can simplify the phrase \"$x$ is an integer and $x$ is an integer\" to just \"$x$ is an integer\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is an integer, and it is negative.\"\n\nFinally, we can write the sentence more concisely:\n\n\"$x$ is a negative integer.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198689 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198252 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2993b4ab-e45b-579a-8a11-b5e9ee107d5b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41dde3e3-6092-50d7-a3e3-9b03129714b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381363} {:answer/id #uuid "ab38e2e3-7aa0-5681-bd79-b716a1f5ebfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(P∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381364} {:answer/id #uuid "765bffbf-d84a-5ff5-a5f8-870a92ad58fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381365} {:answer/id #uuid "63cf5e8f-593a-5960-b49a-27fd32e7eff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧(Q∨P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381366} {:answer/id #uuid "1b83a791-8241-5cd5-855b-476449665c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b83a791-8241-5cd5-855b-476449665c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381367} :answer-field/id #uuid "b22e7a73-f4cf-5a91-83ba-e94d101da87b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381362}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7ff7b2b7-dfb5-55b1-bfd4-172f42c8239c" :question/math-academy-id "q-170725" :question/problem "$x$ is even **or** odd.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is even\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is odd" :question/worked-solution "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{x\\text{ is odd}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∨Q.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381368 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198252 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2993b4ab-e45b-579a-8a11-b5e9ee107d5b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "443c2ac2-d73e-5209-b21f-beb333bf7d18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨(A∧B)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381370} {:answer/id #uuid "ea606823-2fa9-5cc2-990c-5045edd76dfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381371} {:answer/id #uuid "8c7ab119-0282-5fbe-9bf9-0e338586bd6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∧(B∨A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381372} {:answer/id #uuid "8d3b63ed-53f9-5121-b506-5b94b2f06ab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∧B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381373} {:answer/id #uuid "baa4f7d6-0324-5b7e-8071-793d1a8bec13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B∧B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea606823-2fa9-5cc2-990c-5045edd76dfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381371} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc686a5e-3a2b-5cc8-ad6d-1246bf1f5079" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "694a195b-decb-5476-962c-92767f80b122" :question/math-academy-id "q-170735" :question/problem "$x$ is rational  **or** greater than $10.$\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $A(x):$ $x$ is rational\n\n- $B(x):$ $x$ is greater than $10$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is rational}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{x>10}_{⏟}}_{B},\n$$\n\nthat is, $A∨B.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426839 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198253 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce659c55-ca26-52c6-b15e-ec317013d856" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Nested Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19fe9774-58ed-565f-9cbb-223d3c49f77e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(X∨Y)∨Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426814} {:answer/id #uuid "975840e4-95b6-570a-bca6-50be4fce0c45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(X∨Y)∧Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426824} {:answer/id #uuid "bda4b648-d128-5a9f-af66-b574da891c6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X∨(Y∧Z)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426830} {:answer/id #uuid "c69e7e45-595b-57f9-9f1e-7da09afbdb28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(X∧Y)∨Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426832} {:answer/id #uuid "f8d36d58-81e3-5ce6-a949-0b1fb3544fff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X∧(Y∧Z)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "975840e4-95b6-570a-bca6-50be4fce0c45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(X∨Y)∧Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426824} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb8b0f6c-4a71-5c9b-bc62-54e3ad24cf0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17d0f2d8-abc7-53ff-a964-9b193b159c69" :question/math-academy-id "q-170742" :question/problem "$n$ is less than $10$ **or** $13$, **and** $n$ is an integer\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $X(n):$ $n$ is less than $10$\n\n- $Y(n):$ $n$ is less than $13$\n\n- $Z(n):$ $n$ is an integer" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧,$\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:  \n\n- **Part 1:** $n$ is less than $10$ or $13.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{n\\text{ is less than }10}_{⏟}}_{X}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{n\\text{ is less than }13}_{⏟}}_{Y},\n$$\n\nthat is, $X∨Y.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $n$ is an integer. This corresponds to $Z.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{n\\text{ is less than }10\\text{ or }13}_{⏟}}_{X∨Y}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{n\\text{ is an integer}}_{⏟}}_{Z},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(X∨Y)∧Z.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426838 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198255 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f674fcf-7f3e-53c0-8759-6f83b0820160" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Conjunction and Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5350a4a4-f298-59d8-9612-4c7517461dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$y$ is irrational or negative but not both." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426817} {:answer/id #uuid "7d17b8f6-c501-5b6a-9f25-24fb0da0b825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$y$ is irrational or negative." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426819} {:answer/id #uuid "8724cd76-5bf1-5bcc-bde0-4e58af383bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$y$ is irrational." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426820} {:answer/id #uuid "97073a41-e9c9-5ba0-a4bd-c3da3d9761ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$y$ is irrational and negative." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426823} {:answer/id #uuid "ae7c50ca-e9d1-5f38-8f63-d041811dcbb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$y$ is negative." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d17b8f6-c501-5b6a-9f25-24fb0da0b825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$y$ is irrational or negative." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426819} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef163c6e-9635-5101-b558-ea7a832bcdd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0d9b6544-a3d6-5482-a66b-0b543948f593" :question/math-academy-id "q-171040" :question/problem "Simplify the following sentence: \"$y$ is irrational and it is an irrational number, or $y$ is irrational or it is a negative number.\"" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify the phrase \"$y$ is irrational and it is an irrational number\" to just \"$y$ is irrational.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$y$ is irrational, or $y$ is irrational or it is a negative number.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma in the sentence:\n\n\"$y$ is irrational or $y$ is irrational, or it is a negative number.\"\n\nNow, we simplify the phrase \"$y$ is irrational or $y$ is irrational\" to just \"$y$ is irrational.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$y$ is irrational, or it is a negative number.\"\n\nFinally, we simplify the sentence to\n\n\"$y$ is irrational or negative.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381502 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198253 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce659c55-ca26-52c6-b15e-ec317013d856" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Nested Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d99eb173-3abf-5775-a859-5a92ae2ae01f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∨R)∨(P∨I)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381504} {:answer/id #uuid "df7b7424-fa58-5870-87bc-c682e2678be0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∨R)∧(P∨I)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381505} {:answer/id #uuid "28e544d4-09ee-5450-aac7-cedff79d4967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((N∨R)∧P)∨I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381506} {:answer/id #uuid "d99f5091-2095-5600-a488-bf4114dc1018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∧R)∧(P∧I)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381507} {:answer/id #uuid "6dd81fe8-96cc-5534-bfef-3c16765feb7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∧R)∨(P∧I)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df7b7424-fa58-5870-87bc-c682e2678be0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(N∨R)∧(P∨I)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381505} :answer-field/id #uuid "33ea1fa2-4f60-58ac-aee0-0a9d809fa209" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "357fd90c-bc44-5b21-9839-d55874391b78" :question/math-academy-id "q-175377" :question/problem "$x$ is negative **or** rational, **and** $x$ is positive **or** an  integer.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $N(x):$ $x$ is negative\n\n- $R(x):$ $x$ is rational\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is positive\n\n- $I(x):$ $x$ is an integer" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$,\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $x$ is negative **or** rational. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is negative }}_{⏟}}_{N}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{x\\text{ is rational }}_{⏟}}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N∨R.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is positive **or** an integer. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is positive }}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{x\\text{ is an integer }}_{⏟}}_{I},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∨I.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is negative or rational}}_{⏟}}_{N\\,∨\\,R}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{x\\text{ is positive or an integer }}_{⏟}}_{P\\,∨\\,I},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(N∨R)∧(P∨I).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198254 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6bc626a-9517-584c-bf55-8653227f830e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Sets of Conjunctions and Disjunctions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46ea5f59-2e7f-5295-8695-9592bd42ab82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{1,3,5,7,9\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426816} {:answer/id #uuid "550263d1-e585-5aa0-8873-ca1a37d6d639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{3,6\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426818} {:answer/id #uuid "9b251db1-3373-5f6f-983a-96f7fe8666bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All positive odd integers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426825} {:answer/id #uuid "a9428b0b-b88e-5b0f-a9db-05a9a71468a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{1,3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426827} {:answer/id #uuid "b35083dd-72dd-533d-9726-6630eec2aaae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{1,2,3,4,6,12\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9428b0b-b88e-5b0f-a9db-05a9a71468a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{1,3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426827} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b76c296-5c89-50a5-b725-0525be121d8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "82d493f7-be8a-5b02-922e-c52bcfe9d8a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-175552" :question/problem "Find the truth set of $P(x)∧Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the set of positive integers:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is odd\n\n- $Q(x):$ $12$ is divisible by $x$" :question/worked-solution "The truth set of $P(x)∧Q(x)$ represents the *intersection* of the truth sets of $P(x)$ and $Q(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P∧Q}={T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}\n$$\n\nWe start by finding the truth sets of $P(x)$ and $Q(x):$ \n\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is the set of all positive odd integers, i.e.,\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=\\{1,3,5,7,9,11,13…\\}.\n$$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{Q}=\\{1,2,3,4,6,12\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P∧Q} & ={T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q} \\\\  & =\\{1,3,5,7,9,11,13…\\}\\cap \\{1,2,3,4,6,12\\} \\\\  & =\\{1,3\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389790 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198254 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6bc626a-9517-584c-bf55-8653227f830e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Sets of Conjunctions and Disjunctions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20ec4788-c9fa-5856-aa79-ed932a7b324d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9f/9fc6aa4f7f220a14f33ed6269d598dd7aae24f6efac4caf80c8e7f5386450a5a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389792} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc1c924-ac4a-5694-9ff3-76277fe7d08c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/78/781bd7c0c99aa965c5b20b6545e1ab76acbbc88d7698fbed1afe3e7a6d22a14c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389793} {:answer/id #uuid "ef857f1a-d365-55c1-9f94-4a0e4c46efc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1a/1ab3b9c6a9a4b9f7bb4c481770e9fbf2beec8998eda65d22418535dca31d58bc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389794} {:answer/id #uuid "88e6a03c-020e-515c-97ad-a0dbc44a2bc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ef/efa51ca7fcb2e24c5f7a77114a7accb008696dd012d60307937c26c1039e6892.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389795} {:answer/id #uuid "8944f4c5-55a9-51e1-a1e9-7dc77668ffb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/de/de4621c16bad151116f6c6fa4b197c6207b527bff90e5f9c857405ca3e6b135d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20ec4788-c9fa-5856-aa79-ed932a7b324d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9f/9fc6aa4f7f220a14f33ed6269d598dd7aae24f6efac4caf80c8e7f5386450a5a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389792} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d9db75d-b8b1-5171-a35a-f70bc057c59e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389791}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4eda50f7-a585-5a86-9e62-dbc7c5c300f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-177645" :question/problem "![](images/76/761e02a7613e2d1df4722b7bf6f0a7e1d0b5e7b6dec09d205a1e72a29b8c5eb8.png)\n\nThe shaded regions above represent the truth sets of the predicates $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y),$ defined over the universal set ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following is the truth set of $P∨Q?$" :question/worked-solution "The truth set of $P∨Q$ represents the *union* of the truth sets of $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P∨Q}={T}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to get the truth set of $P(x,y)∨Q(x,y),$ we take all the points that belong to ${T}_{P}$ or ${T}_{Q},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/9f/9fc6aa4f7f220a14f33ed6269d598dd7aae24f6efac4caf80c8e7f5386450a5a.png)\n\n**Note:** The points where the *solid* line meets the *dashed* curve belong to ${T}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}$ since these points lie in ${T}_{P}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426841 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198255 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f674fcf-7f3e-53c0-8759-6f83b0820160" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Conjunction and Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46192eea-f4ae-5745-ab2b-1935f29c22a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z$ is rational or positive but not both" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426815} {:answer/id #uuid "9046c2c1-c0ee-5e13-92fe-5436918ed8ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z$ is rational or positive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426821} {:answer/id #uuid "91799f63-a171-5d71-abd6-d2ac6eb622bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z$ is rational" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426822} {:answer/id #uuid "a892fa0b-ae64-5844-bb4e-4a9d0eb3ece7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z$ is rational and positive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426826} {:answer/id #uuid "c455468d-3494-592f-8fea-f7eb970fc2bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z$ is positive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9046c2c1-c0ee-5e13-92fe-5436918ed8ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z$ is rational or positive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426821} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd4aac9d-4227-5875-926d-41c64f7175cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426836}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "be776820-4de7-562d-ad85-1f2cc185142d" :question/math-academy-id "q-177759" :question/problem "Simplify the following sentence: \"$z$ is rational and it is a rational number, or $z$ is rational or it is a positive number.\"" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify the phrase \"$z$ is rational and it is a rational number\" to just \"$z$ is rational.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$z$ is rational, or $z$ is rational or it is a positive number.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma in the sentence:\n\n\"$z$ is rational or $z$ is rational, or it is a positive number.\"\n\nNow, we simplify the phrase \"$z$ is rational or $z$ is rational\" to just \"$z$ is rational.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$z$ is rational, or it is a positive number.\"\n\nFinally, we simplify the sentence to\n\n\"$z$ is rational or positive.\""}]}
